## Work tracking and triage

Beads (`br`) is the shared durable work record. Use `br` and
`bvr --robot-*`; never parse or hand-edit issue JSONL or initialize a tracker
implicitly. A specific user request takes precedence over automatic selection.

Every mutation has an attributable current-session actor. Claim atomically,
finish your own claims first, and respect other agents' work. Recommendation
requests produce recommendations; implementation requires a request to proceed.
Follow the workflow reference for bounded queries, vocabulary and close evidence.

## Architecture and lifecycle

{{confirmed_architecture_boundaries_or_first_task_design_constraints}}

Separate transformations, validation and state transitions from external I/O.
Mutable state, background work and acquired resources have explicit owners and
cleanup. Imports define APIs; construction/start/disposal own side effects.
Split responsibilities when they diverge, without speculative extension points.

## Errors and validation

Validate external inputs before changing state. Preserve useful causes
internally and sanitize them at presentation boundaries. Expected failures
follow the selected language's explicit error conventions. Never silently
swallow errors or turn failed validation into success with a fallback.

{{project_specific_input_and_error_boundaries}}

## Security

Keep credentials and sensitive payloads out of code, logs, tests and commits.
Use explicit trust boundaries for files, processes, network peers and external
input where applicable. A new dependency needs a concrete gap and a review of
its maintenance and security implications.

{{project_specific_security_constraints}}

## Editing and completion

Inspect Git status first and preserve unrelated changes. Make focused edits;
never stash another person's work or run destructive Git/filesystem operations
without explicit authorization.

Follow the testing reference for meaningful behavior changes and refactors.
Update affected public documentation and contracts with the implementation.
Change generated artifacts through their source and verify their consumers.
Do not treat syntax checks as runtime evidence or planned checks as passing.

Record unfinished work and completion evidence in Beads. Flush explicitly
before handoff or an authorized commit. Commit/push only when authorized, staging
named task-owned paths and relevant issue records.
